s kind independently when applying events, so both decode and ledger enforce rules at their own layers—that's acceptable overlap. I'm cross-checking the service test cases covering broken JSON, empty IDs, invalid kinds, and negative amounts to make sure every bad input path is handled.\n\nNow I'm fixing report.Format to output \"total=N\\n\" properly, and updating service.go to skip blank lines in the input.\n\nI'm wiring up main.go to read stdin, run the batch process, and exit with a nonzero status code on error.\n\nI'm checking whether `batch.go` needs changes too—it just splits input by newline and delegates to service.Run, which will now handle skipping blank lines, so this should already satisfy the batch test cases with empty lines interspersed.\n\nChecking the ledger test logic: credit adds to the total, debit subtracts, and repeated credits with the same id are idempotent—my implementation matches this expected behavior, and the service test sequence should also produce the correct final total. Now I'm ready to implement all the fixes.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":822,"cache_read_input_tokens":17916,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":822},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f068f71a-d8b2-4f1b-a4c1-8ba883c612a1","uuid":"5d3df761-1d09-4226-be1e-83eff339c639"}
